{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.UnifiedIterativeCorrection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.UnifiedIterativeCorrection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_iterative_correction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_iterative_correction","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L242-L249","doc":"Convenience name matching the proposition label.\nSingle-partition (2,2) instance at the historical `w_(2,2)` scale; see\n`stepDelta`'s docstring and `unified_telescope_resolvent` for the live one. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:unified-iterative-correction","label":"prop:unified-iterative-correction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_telescope_resolvent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_telescope_resolvent","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L224-L240","doc":"**The resolvent-damped accumulator telescopes.**\n\nThe per-partition total is `m_e · H_q(λ) · y_λ · ρ_λ(s_*) · (L_A − ln d_λ)` —\nexactly the closed form `prop:unified-iterative-correction` now displays, and\nthe identity that lets the producer's total be reconstructed from the final\ntrace alone (verified to rel 2.7e-63 in the probe). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDeltaResolvent_eq_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDeltaResolvent_eq_partition","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L210-L222","doc":"**The resolvent occupies the weight slot.**\n\nThe live scale is the general per-partition shape with `y_λ` replaced by\n`y_λ · ρ_λ(s_*)`, so every structural result already proved about\n`stepDeltaPartition` transfers verbatim.  This is why adding the omitted factor\nto the content block is a restatement rather than a new derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDeltaResolvent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDeltaResolvent","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L204-L208","doc":"Per-partition per-step contribution at the **live** scale:\n`ΔB_λ = m_e · H_q(λ) · y_λ · ρ_λ(s_*) · (L_k − L_{k−1})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qResolvent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qResolvent","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L199-L202","doc":"The `q`-resolvent on the `λ`-block: `ρ_λ(s) = 1 / (μ_λ + s)`, with `μ_λ` the\nJucys–Murphy `q`-Casimir eigenvalue.  The block-diagonal scalar of\n`def:q-resolvent`'s `R_q(s) = (s + Δ̂_q)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_telescope_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_telescope_partition","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L168-L178","doc":"Per-partition telescoping: total contribution of a single partition λ\nis m_e · H_q(λ) · y_λ · (L_A − L_0).  This holds for every λ, so the\ntotal unified correction is the sum over all enumerated partitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.Delta22_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.Delta22_eq","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L162-L166","doc":"The categorical Wigner scale Δ_(2,2) = m_e · [3]_q · [2]_q². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qHookProduct22_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qHookProduct22_eq","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L157-L160","doc":"The (2,2) q-hook product equals [3]_q · [2]_q² (the hook lengths\nof the 2×2 Young diagram are {3, 2, 2, 1} — and [1]_q = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.unified_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L146-L153","doc":"Total unified correction: B_unified = Δ_(2,2) · w_(2,2) · (L_A − ln 2),\nwhere L_0 = ln |tr I| = ln dim((2,2)) = ln 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.step_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.step_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L137-L144","doc":"The accumulator telescopes: Σ_{k=1..A} (L_k − L_{k-1}) = L_A − L_0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDelta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDelta","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L122-L135","doc":"(2,2) instance of the per-partition step delta, at the **historical**\nWedderburn-weighted scale `m_e · H_q((2,2)) · w_(2,2)`.\n\nThis is neither of the two scales `hecke_core_legacy` carries: the\nsuperseded `C_lambda_kerov_MeV = w_λ · y_λ · H_q · m_e` (`:535`) nor the\nlive `C_lambda_resolvent_MeV = H_q · y_λ · ρ_λ(s_*) · m_e` (`:548`) — it\nomits `y_λ` entirely.  Kept because the telescoping theorems stated about\nit are true of it; for the scale the producer actually applies, and which\n`prop:unified-iterative-correction` now states, use `stepDeltaResolvent`\nbelow.  (Resolved 2026-09-12 under the owner's ruling *\"resolve functionals\n... what lean provable\"*; audit\n`docs/audits/2026-09-12-uic-functional-resolution.md`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDeltaPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.stepDeltaPartition","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L115-L120","doc":"Per-partition per-step contribution:\nΔB_λ = m_e · H_q(λ) · y_λ · (L_k − L_{k−1}),\nthe log-derivative of the running YSN trace in λ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.shadowPrice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.shadowPrice","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L98-L113","doc":"Per-partition weight (prop:mass-coefficient-shadow-price):\ny_λ = w_λ / d_λ − 1/[k]_q!.\nThe constant 1/[k]_q! is the SMALLEST w_λ/d_λ across partitions\nof k, attained by the trivial 1-dim sym/alt reps with\nw = 1/[k]_q! and d = 1.\n\nDocstring corrected 2026-09-05 (owner ruling; PR #6752): it called\nthat constant \"the LP normalisation dual\".  It is not.  The\nnet-constraint dual of prop:operator-selection-lp is identically\nzero — the NF basis contains the identity, so the first Frobenius\nrow is the objective vector and the optimum is 0 for every\nn_target (commit 6b7d2ec4a8; Lean `y_0_eq_zero_of_radical`).\nNothing below changes: `shadowPrice` is and was the displayed\nclosed form, and no theorem in this file depends on the reading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.w22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.w22","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L93-L94","doc":"Wedderburn weight w_{(2,2)} = d_q² / [4]_q!. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.dq22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.dq22","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The q-dimension of (2,2) is d_q = [4]_q! / H_q((2,2))\n= ([1]·[2]·[3]·[4]) / ([3]·[2]²)\n= [4] · [1] / [2] = [4] / [2] = q² + q⁻²  (when [2] ≠ 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qFact4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qFact4","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L83-L85","doc":"[4]_q! = [1]·[2]·[3]·[4]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.chi22_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.chi22_generator","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L72-L79","doc":"Character χ_{(2,2)}(σ_j) = q − q⁻¹ for every Hecke generator σ_j,\nj ∈ {1,2,3}.  This is a class-function fact: the eigenvalues of\nσ_1 and σ_3 are (q, −q⁻¹) (diagonal) and tr(σ_2) = sum of the\ntwo diagonal entries of the mixing matrix, which also equals h.\n\nFor the purposes of the unified accumulator, only the value h\nmatters; the proof reduces to algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.dim22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.dim22","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L68-L70","doc":"The (2,2) partition has dimension 2 (two standard Young\ntableaux: [[1,2],[3,4]] and [[1,3],[2,4]]). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.Delta22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.Delta22","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L62-L64","doc":"The (2,2) Wigner energy scale: Δ_(2,2) = m_e · H_q((2,2)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qHookProduct22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qHookProduct22","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L56-L60","doc":"The q-hook product of the (2,2) partition is [3]_q · [2]_q²,\nobtained from the four hook lengths {3, 2, 2, 1} of the 2×2\nYoung diagram (since [1]_q = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qInt_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qInt_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L43-L54","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical singular-locus-guarded bracket.**\n\nThis site is *not* `qIntBalCl`: it guards the whole singular locus\n`q − q⁻¹ = 0`, so it returns `n` at `q = −1` where the one-sided `qIntBalCl`\nfalls through to `0`.  `qIntBalClSing` is the canonical form with that guard;\nthe agreement is definitional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ConfinedKnotBinding.Unified.qInt","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unified-iterative-correction.lean#L38-L41","doc":"Quantum integer [n]_q = (q^n - q^(-n)) / (q - q^(-1)) over a field F. ","signatureChunk":0}]}